# Fibonacci using Recursion

## Problem Statement
find the nth recursion.

## Algorithm / Approach
`fib(0) = 0`, `fib(1) = 1`, `fib(n) = fib(n-1) + fib(n-2)`.

## Pseudocode
```
FIB(n):
    if n <= 1: return n
    return FIB(n - 1) + FIB(n - 2)
```

## Flowchart
```mermaid
flowchart TD
    A([Start: FIB n]) --> B{n <= 1?}
    B -- Yes --> C[Return n] --> Z([End])
    B -- No --> D[a = FIB n-1]
    D --> E[b = FIB n-2]
    E --> F[Return a + b] --> Z
```

## Recursion Tree (n = 5)
```
                    fib(5)
                  /        \
             fib(4)        fib(3)
            /     \        /    \
        fib(3)  fib(2)  fib(2) fib(1)
        /   \
    fib(2) fib(1)   ...  (fib(3), fib(2) baar-baar repeat)
```

## Time & Space Complexity
| | |
|---|---|
| Time | **O(2ⁿ)** (precisely ~ φⁿ, φ = 1.618) |
| Space | O(n) (recursion stack depth) |

Recurrence: `T(n) = T(n-1) + T(n-2) + O(1)`

## Sample Input / Output
```
n = 10
fib(10) = 55
Total recursive calls = 177

n = 35
fib(35) = 9227465
Total recursive calls = 29860703
Time = ~103 ms   
```

